{"overview":"A mature and visually elegant period romance that remains one of the earliest and most compassionate overtly gay-themed films in movie history. Based upon Herman Bang's 1902 novel, Dreyer's Michael refashions the classical Greek myth of Jupiter and Ganymede into a love triangle between an aging artist, Zoret, his protagonist Michael, and Princess Zamikoff, an aristocratic femme fatale as entranced by Michael’s youthful beauty as Zoret is.","cast":[{"n":"Walter Slezak","c":"Eugene Michael","p":"/ilVLhrlP21zvzfQ02vc5Lnj1O64.jpg","q":"Q113328"},{"n":"Benjamin Christensen","c":"Claude Zoret","p":"/uUDlLoJQo9HSai9ldDM3WVZW2r5.jpg","q":"Q817442"},{"n":"Nora Gregor","c":"Princess Lucia Zamikoff","p":"/7hOjInnf0E4G2Ohwz7QPvdamMcj.jpg","q":"Q78887"},{"n":"Max Auzinger","c":"Jules - Majordomo","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Robert Garrison","c":"Charles Switt - Art Critic","p":"/6ZeIJnixBaV7xV5LL6iGMxGt1Q3.jpg","q":"Q119968"},{"n":"Karl Freund","c":"LeBlanc - Art Dealer","p":"/i967rbvQCVKgtX1BV1fCZ9hkd5E.jpg","q":"Q62099"},{"n":"Alexander Murski","c":"Mr. Adelsskjold","p":"/5P0qNC1fiKziVg0O1AUuGHSofLM.jpg","q":"Q1717967"},{"n":"Grete Mosheim","c":"Mrs. Alice Adelsskjold","p":"/Ae8RAXLCrc9JmWu1rYe0cLyDOto.jpg","q":"Q91872"},{"n":"Didier Aslan","c":"Duke Monthieu","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Wilhelmine Sandrock","c":"Dowager Duchess Monthieu","p":null,"q":"Q1755338"}],"country":["Germany"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_(1924_film)","qid":"Q659669","rel":{"DE":{"d":"1924-09-26"},"GR":{"d":"2026-07-16"},"NL":{"d":"2008-07-08"}},"backdrops":["/zJEGBiV1rhnnUo2IxQ1oKMHLqCY.jpg","/pPmcZ1VDaHytOHi86Ay1nOK0Rzm.jpg","/1r0gGKxRc35bwgpu1qeQotbJqQt.jpg","/ahsKxIYoX0jHH7HCx0TWVSQRFfr.jpg","/njo5Rj8kQd5qANOCSNWdlNuYmzv.jpg","/wqRYG1zgIktn7hSqnLCtZeGIb4S.jpg","/7cWcSA6KiCCXWncifROhFRD9phx.jpg","/7PDdWnPq6s49PBleoyUIZNzvbbn.jpg"]}